WEBVTT

00:06.589 --> 00:07.507
Come on, Taiga!

00:07.590 --> 00:09.426
Don't fall behind!

00:11.511 --> 00:13.555
Keep up or you'll lose!

00:17.851 --> 00:20.353
Even if our ace runner buys us time,
there's no point

00:20.854 --> 00:22.939
if everyone else wastes it.

00:24.733 --> 00:25.650
Taiga.

00:27.777 --> 00:29.195
You're off the team.

00:33.158 --> 00:36.202
- Man, that's brutal.
- Poor guy.

00:36.286 --> 00:37.746
He didn't make it after all.

02:01.746 --> 02:03.790
‪TANOMI

02:03.873 --> 02:06.126
So you're going
to tour properties together?

02:07.752 --> 02:10.880
Yeah. We're going on our next day off.

02:12.924 --> 02:14.509
You don't waste any time, huh?

02:14.592 --> 02:16.219
It's not what you're thinking.

02:16.302 --> 02:19.722
I'm only going for moral support.

02:19.806 --> 02:21.724
Are you stupid?

02:21.808 --> 02:24.894
You think she'd tour properties with a guy
who's not her parent or boyfriend?

02:29.941 --> 02:30.859
You think so?

02:30.942 --> 02:32.527
- Shige.
- Huh?

02:32.610 --> 02:34.529
Taiga is about to get a girlfriend.

02:34.612 --> 02:37.407
- Noa! It's not like that!
- I didn't expect that.

02:37.490 --> 02:38.908
Like I said, it's not like that.

02:40.243 --> 02:42.704
And plus, even if it was,

02:42.787 --> 02:44.581
our relationship wouldn't go anywhere.

02:45.331 --> 02:46.332
Why?

02:47.667 --> 02:49.794
She's an international student from Korea,

02:50.378 --> 02:52.463
so she shouldn't be with someone like me.

02:53.006 --> 02:54.465
Someone like you?

02:54.549 --> 02:55.925
I mean…

02:56.509 --> 02:58.845
Someone with no future.

03:01.514 --> 03:02.849
So you're saying

03:02.932 --> 03:05.935
that a restaurant employee
is going to accompany you?

03:08.771 --> 03:12.150
Yes, um…

03:12.817 --> 03:14.819
Kind of like a Japanese advisor.

03:17.030 --> 03:19.699
Taiga isn't suspicious at all.

03:19.782 --> 03:22.410
He came with me
out of the kindness of his heart.

03:22.493 --> 03:23.328
‪KAEDE REAL ESTATE

03:23.411 --> 03:24.537
All right.

03:24.621 --> 03:28.750
Well then, let me suggest some
properties that might fit your taste.

03:28.833 --> 03:30.251
Thank you.

03:30.835 --> 03:34.797
I picked out a few
that fit your requirements.

03:34.881 --> 03:35.840
In your case,

03:35.924 --> 03:40.637
the trickiest part
is that you have to move out in one year.

03:41.471 --> 03:44.515
Well, why don't we take
a tour of them first?

03:50.438 --> 03:51.314
Well…

03:52.649 --> 03:54.776
You're leaving in a year, huh?

03:55.276 --> 03:56.361
Yes.

03:56.444 --> 03:58.821
If I can actually graduate, that is.

04:00.448 --> 04:02.617
My student visa is going to expire,

04:02.700 --> 04:06.746
so I can't stay in Japan
unless I start working.

04:07.247 --> 04:08.414
Oh, your visa?

04:09.165 --> 04:11.209
Wow, that's amazing.

04:12.710 --> 04:13.795
Amazing?

04:14.379 --> 04:16.089
What about it is amazing?

04:18.258 --> 04:21.261
Well, just talking about visas and stuff

04:21.344 --> 04:23.471
is amazing from my point of view.

04:24.764 --> 04:27.141
It's like you're talking about
a whole different world.

04:27.725 --> 04:29.686
There's nothing amazing about it.

04:30.311 --> 04:33.064
International students
all stay here with student visas,

04:33.147 --> 04:35.358
and go back to Korea once they graduate.

04:35.858 --> 04:37.360
I see…

04:37.986 --> 04:39.445
Of course…

04:39.529 --> 04:41.072
Before that,

04:41.155 --> 04:44.075
I hope I can cross things
off my bucket list.

04:45.493 --> 04:46.869
Bucket list?

04:48.538 --> 04:49.372
Yes.

04:50.081 --> 04:54.627
A list of things that I want to do
before I die.

04:54.711 --> 04:57.672
One item on my bucket list

04:57.755 --> 05:00.758
is to try every kind
of Japanese convenience store snack.

05:01.884 --> 05:02.885
I see.

05:03.636 --> 05:04.929
Interesting.

05:05.013 --> 05:08.141
Why don't you make one too?

05:08.224 --> 05:09.225
What?

05:10.351 --> 05:12.353
I don't think that's necessary.

05:12.437 --> 05:14.105
You agree, right Noa?

05:14.188 --> 05:16.524
But your daughter
is in middle school, right?

05:17.859 --> 05:19.819
Then I guess she'd want a new device.

05:19.902 --> 05:22.363
As long as I can make a call,
that's enough for me.

05:22.447 --> 05:24.407
They're all the same, no?

05:24.490 --> 05:26.659
They are not all the same.

05:26.743 --> 05:28.578
The image quality and stuff are different.

05:28.661 --> 05:29.996
You think so?

05:31.331 --> 05:35.001
So your labor right now is going to turn
into your daughter's smartphone?

05:35.084 --> 05:37.712
That's right. It's ridiculous.

05:37.795 --> 05:41.507
I wish she'd just keep using
the one she's used to.

05:55.438 --> 05:58.524
I don't know… It's pretty nice but…

05:58.608 --> 05:59.984
What do you think?

06:05.782 --> 06:07.450
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

06:07.533 --> 06:11.871
Does a lot of smoke rise up
from the restaurants below?

06:14.040 --> 06:16.793
I don't think it'll be a problem,

06:17.376 --> 06:18.961
but I can ask about it.

06:19.045 --> 06:20.088
Okay, thank you.

06:22.840 --> 06:25.093
The placement of the exhaust fans
might be an issue.

06:27.095 --> 06:28.679
I didn't notice that at all.

06:36.979 --> 06:37.814
Oh, Taiga.

06:39.357 --> 06:41.859
- Can I ask you something?
- Yes.

06:41.943 --> 06:45.655
This room doesn't have a refrigerator
or washing machine or anything.

06:46.989 --> 06:49.826
Rooms in Korea usually come
with appliances.

06:49.909 --> 06:51.285
Oh really?

06:52.703 --> 06:54.539
Well, it's not like
anything is wrong here.

06:54.622 --> 06:57.333
In Japan, this is normal.

06:58.084 --> 06:59.127
Oh, good.

06:59.210 --> 07:02.672
If you have any questions,
don't hesitate to ask me.

07:03.840 --> 07:05.341
Thank you.

07:10.513 --> 07:11.931
These windows are cute!

07:14.976 --> 07:16.644
The kitchen is big too.

07:19.063 --> 07:20.398
I like this place.

07:22.817 --> 07:24.777
This is a really nice place.

07:25.319 --> 07:29.115
I agree. The rent is not too high either.

07:29.198 --> 07:31.033
I like it a lot.

07:31.534 --> 07:33.744
I think my mind is set on this one.

07:34.871 --> 07:36.414
Wait a second.

07:50.178 --> 07:51.721
No issues with the security either.

07:59.020 --> 08:01.022
Thank you for today.

08:01.105 --> 08:03.566
I found a nice place thanks to you.

08:03.649 --> 08:05.443
I didn't do anything.

08:06.110 --> 08:07.904
I'm glad you found a place.

08:09.489 --> 08:13.117
I hope they accept my application.

08:15.286 --> 08:17.955
It'll be fine. I'm sure.

08:24.962 --> 08:26.172
Taiga.

08:27.924 --> 08:29.675
Today, I…

08:31.427 --> 08:33.012
had a lot of fun.

08:36.432 --> 08:39.101
Looking at houses is fun, isn't it?

08:43.940 --> 08:45.233
Um…

08:46.901 --> 08:51.614
STRAWBERRY CARAMEL

08:57.411 --> 09:00.456
This is a thank you gift for today.

09:00.540 --> 09:01.624
Here you go.

09:09.340 --> 09:10.883
Thank you.

09:16.847 --> 09:18.099
Well, see you…

09:19.600 --> 09:20.643
Right…

09:22.728 --> 09:25.606
Well then… See you.

09:57.847 --> 10:00.683
You should give up on Onigiri Man.

10:00.766 --> 10:02.935
We had a good vibe,

10:03.019 --> 10:04.770
so why didn't he ask me out
on another date?

10:06.105 --> 10:07.648
Did I do something wrong?

10:08.316 --> 10:09.567
That's not it.

10:09.650 --> 10:11.861
Didn't I tell you before?

10:12.862 --> 10:14.739
Japanese men are extremely reserved

10:14.822 --> 10:18.367
when it comes to expressing
their feelings.

10:18.451 --> 10:20.578
Isn't that just your opinion?

10:21.078 --> 10:22.663
Park Rin!

10:22.747 --> 10:25.124
How many times do I have to tell you?

10:25.750 --> 10:28.753
I am a professional content buyer, okay?

10:28.836 --> 10:33.633
I've watched
all the movies and dramas to death.

10:33.716 --> 10:35.301
But dramas are just dramas.

10:35.384 --> 10:36.218
What are you saying!

10:36.302 --> 10:41.599
Dramas reflect
the culture of that country.

10:41.682 --> 10:43.517
According to my database,

10:43.601 --> 10:47.647
main characters in Japanese dramas
are more sensitive.

10:47.730 --> 10:52.693
In many stories, they overthink everything
and don't even get together in the end.

10:54.070 --> 10:55.029
Really?

10:56.030 --> 10:57.198
Yes.

10:58.991 --> 11:03.454
Dating someone of a different nationality
isn't easy.

11:03.537 --> 11:05.414
So don't try to rush into it
unnecessarily.

11:08.334 --> 11:09.502
Yeah?

11:10.086 --> 11:11.629
Park Rin.

11:11.712 --> 11:13.381
If you keep acting like that,

11:13.464 --> 11:15.925
- I will tell your mother.
- Don't you dare!

11:17.301 --> 11:20.012
Fine. I'll stop.

11:21.430 --> 11:24.475
I'm here to study, after all.

11:24.558 --> 11:26.018
That's right.

11:27.812 --> 11:29.605
I have to go. Bye!

11:30.314 --> 11:31.732
Enjoy the party.

11:34.110 --> 11:36.654
- How has your mother been lately?
- Who knows?

11:37.613 --> 11:40.241
I'm sure she's having fun with a guy,
as usual.

11:40.324 --> 11:42.284
It's okay, I'll do it myself.

11:43.494 --> 11:45.413
She'll show up when she feels like it.

11:46.914 --> 11:48.165
You're okay with that?

11:50.292 --> 11:52.795
I don't have any other choice, do I?

11:53.921 --> 11:55.131
More importantly,

11:56.215 --> 11:57.800
are you serious about what you said?

11:58.676 --> 12:02.054
Well, ever since I started,
I've been preparing myself

12:03.681 --> 12:06.308
for the possibility of closing
the restaurant when I retire.

12:09.478 --> 12:12.440
Hey, if you're going to retire,

12:13.357 --> 12:14.817
why not have Taiga take over?

12:15.776 --> 12:18.195
That would be a lot to ask of him.

12:18.779 --> 12:19.613
You think so?

12:27.121 --> 12:29.540
I didn't pass the contest again.

12:30.249 --> 12:31.417
What about you?

12:31.500 --> 12:33.335
I didn't make it either.

12:39.341 --> 12:40.176
I heard Amane

12:40.759 --> 12:43.179
is going to have her solo exhibition
in New York.

12:43.679 --> 12:44.763
She's making figurines too.

12:46.724 --> 12:47.766
Wow.

12:47.850 --> 12:50.227
When you have that much talent,

12:50.311 --> 12:51.979
I bet you don't
have to worry about your future.

12:52.062 --> 12:55.274
After graduating, she can just go
straight into the professional world.

12:57.026 --> 12:59.361
I have to decide on what to do myself.

13:00.029 --> 13:04.033
Rin, you're going back to Korea
and not finding a job over here, right?

13:04.825 --> 13:08.537
For the most part, that's my plan…

13:09.079 --> 13:10.706
I'm so jealous.

13:10.789 --> 13:13.709
Maybe I'll follow you and go to Korea too?

13:13.792 --> 13:14.919
Just kidding.

13:33.354 --> 13:34.396
Thank you for the food.

13:43.822 --> 13:44.698
That's delicious.

13:47.535 --> 13:49.119
What is this dish called?

13:49.703 --> 13:52.706
Today, it's Pacific Barrelfish
cooked in a bamboo steamer.

13:53.541 --> 13:55.751
It's a white fish,
but it's nice and fatty, right?

13:55.834 --> 13:59.421
When it's freshly caught,
the skin is greasy.

13:59.505 --> 14:00.798
Greasy?

14:01.882 --> 14:05.135
Is that different from "slimy"?

14:05.844 --> 14:07.805
Well, it's basically in the same family.

14:07.888 --> 14:10.933
You're so knowledgeable.
You're amazing, Master.

14:11.016 --> 14:14.228
A cook should be knowledgeable
about his ingredients.

14:14.853 --> 14:18.399
Even when I go to an aquarium,
I know almost all the fish there.

14:18.482 --> 14:19.942
Really? Wow.

14:21.861 --> 14:25.114
That reminds me…
I haven't been to an aquarium in ages.

14:25.197 --> 14:26.365
Oh really?

14:27.616 --> 14:29.201
You should have someone take you.

14:33.747 --> 14:35.082
Hey.

14:35.165 --> 14:37.126
If you want to, just ask her.

14:37.960 --> 14:39.420
What are you talking about?

14:39.503 --> 14:42.298
You've been staring at her the whole time.

14:42.923 --> 14:46.218
- I was not staring.
- You were staring at her like a creep.

14:46.760 --> 14:48.387
You were eavesdropping too, right?

14:49.430 --> 14:51.390
Hurry up and take this chance.

14:53.559 --> 14:57.396
But she said she's going back
to Korea in a year.

14:57.479 --> 14:59.899
Even if I ask her to go with me,
it'll only trouble her.

14:59.982 --> 15:01.692
Yeah, yeah… Just go!

15:07.948 --> 15:08.991
Um…

15:09.909 --> 15:10.868
Yes?

15:11.619 --> 15:16.081
I overheard
that you haven't been to an aquarium.

15:16.707 --> 15:17.791
Yes.

15:17.875 --> 15:20.044
I haven't been to one since I was a child.

15:23.297 --> 15:24.506
If you…

15:26.342 --> 15:29.595
happen to have a day
where you have absolutely nothing to do,

15:30.304 --> 15:33.265
- would you like to go to an aquarium--
- Yes.

15:34.683 --> 15:36.560
Huh? Really?

15:37.519 --> 15:38.812
I'd love to go.

15:39.438 --> 15:40.606
Let's go together.

15:51.241 --> 15:53.619
AKINORI: I'M OUT OF MONEY!
COME TO THE PACHINKO PARLOR!

15:57.122 --> 15:58.207
Yes.

16:10.386 --> 16:11.428
How is it going?

16:11.512 --> 16:13.597
I'm definitely going to win big.

16:13.681 --> 16:14.890
I know it.

16:15.391 --> 16:16.558
- Really?
- Yeah.

16:17.142 --> 16:19.061
No doubt about it.

16:21.730 --> 16:22.564
Please?

16:26.652 --> 16:28.112
Fine…

16:29.697 --> 16:30.906
‪10000 YEN

16:32.241 --> 16:34.243
- Here.
- Thank you, Noa.

16:34.743 --> 16:36.662
Let's go eat yakiniku or sushi today.

16:37.746 --> 16:40.082
- All right. I'll look forward to it.
- Okay.

16:40.165 --> 16:41.625
- Good luck.
- Thanks.

16:48.382 --> 16:49.633
All right!

17:01.061 --> 17:04.481
HOW ABOUT THIS AQUARIUM?

17:04.565 --> 17:09.445
DOES THE 24TH OR 25TH WORK FOR YOU?

17:10.029 --> 17:12.448
AQUA WORLD

17:16.577 --> 17:18.662
It's pretty big.

17:18.746 --> 17:21.331
The sea lion show is once every two hours.

17:21.415 --> 17:22.916
So start with penguins…

17:24.752 --> 17:26.587
And after that…

17:41.727 --> 17:43.395
BIG BRO - I WAS PROMOTED TO SECTION CHIEF

17:43.479 --> 17:44.938
MOM - YOUR HARD WORK PAID OFF

17:48.525 --> 17:50.027
Taiga. You're off the team.

17:50.110 --> 17:51.945
He got an endorsement and he's a reserve?

17:52.029 --> 17:53.864
Are you going to Tokyo to run away?

17:53.947 --> 17:55.074
Are you really sure?

17:55.157 --> 17:56.700
He didn't make it after all.

18:11.298 --> 18:13.550
TICKET

18:14.259 --> 18:15.969
All right.

18:26.605 --> 18:28.023
ITINERARY

18:28.107 --> 18:29.399
PENGUIN POOL - SEA LION SHOW

18:36.198 --> 18:38.909
I'm sorry. Did I make you wait?

18:38.992 --> 18:40.744
Oh, no. Not at all.

18:41.787 --> 18:43.080
Ready to go?

18:43.831 --> 18:44.790
Yes.

18:57.594 --> 18:58.804
Pretty…

18:59.763 --> 19:01.765
Did you want to see any specific fish?

19:03.892 --> 19:06.728
I want to see that thing…

19:07.271 --> 19:08.397
Gaoli.

19:08.480 --> 19:09.523
Kaoli?

19:10.524 --> 19:12.484
Um…

19:13.402 --> 19:16.280
Oh, right. A ray.

19:18.198 --> 19:19.449
A ray?

19:19.533 --> 19:21.451
I want to see the underside of a ray.

19:22.369 --> 19:23.954
Is that called their underside?

19:24.496 --> 19:25.747
It's not?

19:25.831 --> 19:28.709
It looks like a face
and it's kind of cute.

19:28.792 --> 19:30.210
They're always smiling.

19:31.295 --> 19:33.964
Let's make sure we see the rays then.

19:34.047 --> 19:35.799
I'll guide you through the facility,

19:35.883 --> 19:37.467
so you just enjoy yourself.

19:37.551 --> 19:39.136
Thank you.

19:41.847 --> 19:42.848
But…

19:47.519 --> 19:49.605
I want to enjoy it with you.

19:52.441 --> 19:53.400
Yes.

19:53.483 --> 19:55.402
Of course, me too.

19:57.070 --> 19:58.947
Wow! Penguins?

19:59.031 --> 20:02.451
Yes. It's a popular attraction,
and a lot of them swim in the pool.

20:02.534 --> 20:05.078
I saw it on their homepage,
and they were really cute.

20:05.162 --> 20:06.413
- Really?
- Yes.

20:06.496 --> 20:08.040
I can't wait to see.

20:08.832 --> 20:10.000
This is the penguin area.

20:10.083 --> 20:11.210
‪HUMBOLDT PENGUIN

20:17.633 --> 20:20.761
Where are the penguins?

20:28.518 --> 20:29.895
They're not here, huh?

20:30.479 --> 20:31.521
Are they on break?

20:38.278 --> 20:40.364
There's a sea lion show. Want to see that?

20:40.447 --> 20:42.366
Sea lions are really smart and cute.

20:42.449 --> 20:44.826
Yeah. I'm excited.

20:45.702 --> 20:47.246
- It's this way.
- Okay.

20:49.790 --> 20:52.626
How do you say sea lion in Korean?

20:53.377 --> 20:54.586
Mulgae.

20:54.670 --> 20:55.796
Mulgae?

20:55.879 --> 20:57.631
- We will make an announcement soon.
- Mulgae.

20:58.674 --> 20:59.967
We're very sorry.

21:01.009 --> 21:03.178
We apologize.

21:03.262 --> 21:04.346
Excuse me.

21:04.429 --> 21:06.974
We're sorry, but there were some
issues with the tank.

21:07.057 --> 21:08.767
So we're trying to repair it now.

21:08.850 --> 21:10.644
What? Oh no…

21:10.727 --> 21:11.895
We're terribly sorry.

21:11.979 --> 21:13.563
What should we do?

21:15.691 --> 21:19.069
This aquarium is famous
for their special drink. Want to try it?

21:19.152 --> 21:22.114
- Sounds good.
- It's this way.

21:24.157 --> 21:25.158
PENGUIN SODA

21:25.242 --> 21:26.702
How cute!

21:26.785 --> 21:30.789
I'm sorry. We just ran out
of the Penguin Soda.

21:30.872 --> 21:34.376
You've got to be kidding.
We came here expecting to buy this.

21:34.459 --> 21:35.961
You think it's some joke?

21:36.044 --> 21:38.213
You didn't even do the sea lion show.

21:39.131 --> 21:41.842
I can't believe we had to pay
the same entrance fee.

21:42.467 --> 21:43.844
- Let's go.
- Yeah.

21:44.720 --> 21:46.263
I'm very sorry.

21:47.014 --> 21:48.974
Hello, can you take our order?

21:49.474 --> 21:52.269
I'm sorry,
we're out of our special Penguin Soda.

21:52.352 --> 21:55.188
No worries. Must be tough, huh?

22:11.121 --> 22:12.331
I'm sorry.

22:12.914 --> 22:15.208
It's not going as planned at all.

22:15.709 --> 22:16.543
No…

22:17.210 --> 22:20.797
I appreciate how much thought
you put into it.

22:26.094 --> 22:27.304
The sea lion show…

22:27.804 --> 22:29.473
I hope it reopens soon.

22:33.226 --> 22:35.854
BIG BRO

22:41.234 --> 22:43.403
- Give me a second.
- Take your time.

22:48.408 --> 22:51.161
Sorry, I was kind of busy.

22:52.120 --> 22:53.413
What's wrong?

22:54.289 --> 22:57.959
Mom fell at home and hurt herself.

22:58.627 --> 22:59.795
What?

22:59.878 --> 23:01.088
Is she all right?

23:01.171 --> 23:04.007
Yeah, they're taking
a look at her at the hospital.

23:04.091 --> 23:05.634
It wasn't anything serious.

23:06.760 --> 23:08.470
Thank goodness.

23:09.846 --> 23:11.515
You know,

23:12.265 --> 23:14.351
why aren't you looking after the family?

23:14.434 --> 23:15.977
Why do I have to take time off work?

23:17.979 --> 23:19.064
Sorry…

23:21.108 --> 23:23.735
Whatever… We'll take care of it.

23:26.905 --> 23:28.448
Thank you.

23:30.242 --> 23:33.370
You're not young anymore,
so enough of this "self-discovery" stuff.

23:33.870 --> 23:34.913
Bye.

23:42.129 --> 23:45.048
An announcement to all guests.

23:45.132 --> 23:47.175
We are terribly sorry,

23:47.259 --> 23:50.387
but today's sea lion show
will be canceled.

23:52.013 --> 23:54.933
An announcement to all guests.

23:55.016 --> 23:57.227
We are terribly sorry,

23:57.310 --> 24:00.480
but today's sea lion show
will be canceled.

24:07.988 --> 24:11.074
I wish I could've seen
the sea lions with you.

24:11.658 --> 24:12.909
Too bad.

24:16.454 --> 24:17.789
I'm sorry.

24:18.957 --> 24:21.835
This aquarium was supposed to be more fun.

24:22.586 --> 24:24.796
It's not your fault, Taiga.

24:26.214 --> 24:27.424
Well,

24:28.341 --> 24:30.135
I'm used to this, anyway.

24:31.219 --> 24:33.096
Used to what?

24:35.891 --> 24:40.228
Things not going according to plan.

24:42.856 --> 24:46.026
It's true that we've been
out of luck this whole day.

24:46.735 --> 24:51.239
But halfway through, I started to wonder,
"What's going to happen next?"

24:51.823 --> 24:53.658
And that was actually exciting.

24:55.869 --> 24:58.371
It's not that I don't have a plan.

24:59.122 --> 25:02.500
I just can't seem
to follow through with it.

25:07.088 --> 25:11.676
Nothing in my life
has ever gone according to plan.

25:17.349 --> 25:19.059
Compared to that,

25:20.310 --> 25:21.645
you are amazing, Rin.

25:22.437 --> 25:24.189
Why is that?

25:24.272 --> 25:26.483
You came to a foreign country on your own,

25:27.025 --> 25:30.487
and you're moving forward
toward your dream.

25:30.570 --> 25:33.406
You have the ability to take action,

25:33.990 --> 25:35.325
and you have courage.

25:37.911 --> 25:41.456
Did you try making a bucket list?

25:42.666 --> 25:43.583
What?

25:45.627 --> 25:47.504
I don't have any dreams or anything.

25:48.380 --> 25:51.508
It doesn't have to be
something serious like that.

25:52.217 --> 25:56.972
Bucket lists can also help you find goals.

25:58.098 --> 25:59.975
The truth is,

26:00.058 --> 26:02.269
I set up a goal for myself today.

26:04.396 --> 26:06.690
Since you always cook for me,

26:07.190 --> 26:09.401
I wanted to cook for you today.

26:10.986 --> 26:13.530
But it was really hard.

26:15.156 --> 26:16.366
Take a look.

26:21.162 --> 26:24.040
Wow. They're huge.

26:24.124 --> 26:26.876
I thought that might make you happier.

26:29.671 --> 26:32.048
I'm still working on it.

26:36.553 --> 26:38.763
But I did my best.

26:53.695 --> 26:55.363
- Thank you.
- Enjoy.

27:08.918 --> 27:11.212
- It's good.
- Really?

27:13.506 --> 27:14.549
Yes.

27:15.425 --> 27:16.634
I'm glad.

27:20.263 --> 27:21.306
It's good.

27:24.434 --> 27:26.269
It's really good.

27:26.895 --> 27:28.271
Thank you.

27:35.779 --> 27:40.533
Thank you very much for visiting today.

27:41.159 --> 27:43.620
We will be closing soon.

27:44.204 --> 27:45.330
We look forward to…

27:48.333 --> 27:51.169
Taiga! We don't have to go out of our way!

27:51.252 --> 27:53.880
No! We should see the rays.

27:53.963 --> 27:55.924
They're in the biggest tank.

27:57.300 --> 27:58.968
We're almost there.

27:59.469 --> 28:00.303
‪CREATURES OF OARAI

28:02.430 --> 28:04.891
Excuse me. Can we go inside?

28:04.974 --> 28:06.976
Sorry, we closed it off.

28:07.060 --> 28:09.604
Please, let us in!

28:09.687 --> 28:12.273
Rules are rules. Sorry.

28:12.357 --> 28:15.568
Is there no way?
I really want her to see the rays.

28:15.652 --> 28:17.570
We'll leave as soon as we see them.

28:17.654 --> 28:21.366
Once we let a guest in,
the employees have to stay behind.

28:22.700 --> 28:24.411
Right…

28:26.204 --> 28:27.664
Sorry for troubling you.

28:27.747 --> 28:29.040
Sorry about that.

28:29.833 --> 28:31.918
Okay, good bye.

28:35.088 --> 28:36.005
Wait, Sir.

28:39.008 --> 28:42.220
I'll go patrol the other areas,
so during that time,

28:42.303 --> 28:43.513
you can go inside.

28:45.849 --> 28:47.517
Thank you!

28:48.810 --> 28:49.936
There it is!

28:50.019 --> 28:51.521
Gaoli. Ray.

28:52.647 --> 28:54.232
How cute!

28:56.860 --> 28:59.946
I'm so glad you got to see it.

29:05.660 --> 29:07.245
Wow…

29:08.329 --> 29:10.039
We have this place all to ourselves.

29:13.501 --> 29:15.378
We do.

29:44.115 --> 29:45.074
- Taiga.
- Hey…

29:47.535 --> 29:51.039
There is something I want to tell you.

29:54.417 --> 29:55.585
Yes?

30:04.636 --> 30:06.012
- Taiga, I--
- Today,

30:08.890 --> 30:11.476
this date didn't go as planned at all,

30:12.644 --> 30:16.648
and I felt like more and more
of a failure.

30:19.067 --> 30:22.779
But when I'm with you,

30:24.489 --> 30:27.784
I feel a weight off my shoulders.

30:29.869 --> 30:33.540
I feel like I can move forward.

30:47.220 --> 30:48.304
I…

30:50.598 --> 30:52.183
like you,

30:54.227 --> 30:55.436
Rin.

31:03.695 --> 31:06.948
Will you please go out with me?

31:11.744 --> 31:12.704
Yes.

31:34.642 --> 31:36.144
Oh, that reminds me.

31:36.853 --> 31:39.063
I'll give this back to you.

31:41.649 --> 31:42.609
Thank you.

31:43.610 --> 31:45.904
But why now?

31:46.446 --> 31:50.783
Because now I don't need an excuse
to see you anymore.

31:54.203 --> 31:55.121
Thank you.

32:09.844 --> 32:12.305
I can't believe we're dating!

32:13.640 --> 32:15.767
Oh my god! What do I do?

32:25.318 --> 32:29.781
JUN-HO! BIG NEWS!

32:29.864 --> 32:33.660
‪TANOMI

32:34.369 --> 32:35.954
You'll definitely love this place.

32:36.037 --> 32:37.246
Really?

32:37.330 --> 32:38.247
I can't wait.

32:41.000 --> 32:43.836
I'll leave it up to you.
When you're done, I'll taste it.

32:43.920 --> 32:46.005
Okay. Thank you.

32:48.216 --> 32:50.677
- Good evening.
- Welcome.

32:50.760 --> 32:52.470
You came?

32:52.553 --> 32:55.848
Taiga, sorry for interrupting your work.
Do you have a second?

32:55.932 --> 32:57.475
Yes, he does.

32:59.769 --> 33:00.603
You do.

33:06.359 --> 33:07.193
Jun-ho.

33:14.867 --> 33:17.954
Hello. I'm Kang Jun-ho, Rin's senior.

33:18.037 --> 33:19.455
Nice to meet you.

33:22.875 --> 33:23.918
Jun-ho?

33:25.044 --> 33:26.546
Nice to meet you.

33:27.130 --> 33:28.756
I'm Hase Taiga.

33:29.757 --> 33:32.427
He's been helping me since
I was going to college in Korea,

33:32.510 --> 33:34.262
so we've known each other for a long time.

33:34.345 --> 33:37.640
I confide in him a lot.
He's like a dependable older brother.

33:38.224 --> 33:40.476
Oh, really? From college?

33:42.562 --> 33:43.980
And this is…

33:46.482 --> 33:48.901
my boyfriend, Taiga.

33:55.950 --> 33:56.993
He looks nice.

33:57.076 --> 33:58.244
Right?

33:58.327 --> 33:59.829
He's a really good cook too.

34:00.496 --> 34:03.041
Let's have drinks together,

34:03.124 --> 34:05.334
and eat Taiga's cooking today.

34:09.672 --> 34:12.091
Rin, I'm sorry.

34:12.842 --> 34:16.220
There's an emergency
and I have to go back to work.

34:16.304 --> 34:18.014
But you said you finished work…

34:18.097 --> 34:20.933
There was some kind of trouble
and they need me in a hurry.

34:21.851 --> 34:22.685
I'm really sorry.

34:24.312 --> 34:26.105
He said he needs to rush back to work.

34:26.189 --> 34:27.023
What?

34:27.106 --> 34:29.317
I wanted to formally
introduce you guys, but…

34:29.400 --> 34:30.234
I'll go now.

34:40.453 --> 34:41.496
Bye.

35:01.265 --> 35:02.141
That's hot!

35:09.357 --> 35:11.067
What's wrong?

35:11.150 --> 35:13.820
Were you dumped by a girl or something?

35:14.695 --> 35:18.116
Yes. Is it that obvious?

35:18.199 --> 35:20.409
Wow, I was right.

35:20.493 --> 35:23.955
What? Why were you dumped?
You're so good looking.

35:24.038 --> 35:25.581
Did she have a man already?

35:30.169 --> 35:33.923
You just have to steal her away.

35:34.006 --> 35:35.591
I can't do that.

35:36.592 --> 35:38.427
That would make me the worst type of man…

35:43.224 --> 35:45.893
It's okay! It's okay!

35:45.977 --> 35:47.854
That was delicious.

35:47.937 --> 35:50.106
Your cooking is the best.

35:50.189 --> 35:51.107
Thank you.

35:51.190 --> 35:53.568
You really surprised me today, though.

35:54.277 --> 35:57.280
I didn't think you would
bring Jun-ho out of the blue.

35:57.905 --> 35:59.157
What?

35:59.240 --> 36:03.327
I thought it was normal
to introduce my boyfriend to my friend.

36:03.911 --> 36:05.079
Was that weird?

36:05.163 --> 36:06.914
Not at all.

36:07.540 --> 36:10.918
I'm happy you introduced me
to your senior.

36:11.460 --> 36:12.420
Okay, good.

36:13.588 --> 36:14.839
From now on,

36:15.464 --> 36:19.719
let's tell each other whenever something
doesn't feel right.

36:22.263 --> 36:23.139
Of course.

36:24.223 --> 36:26.851
- I promise.
- Don't forget it.

36:45.203 --> 36:46.204
There.

36:52.752 --> 36:54.462
The bucket list thing…

36:55.755 --> 36:57.506
I'm thinking of doing it too.

36:58.299 --> 36:59.425
What?

36:59.508 --> 37:01.344
You found a goal?

37:40.007 --> 37:41.050
This.

37:51.852 --> 37:55.022
That's not what a bucket list is.

37:56.148 --> 37:57.400
Really?

38:02.405 --> 38:05.241
A kiss isn't a life goal, is it?

38:06.284 --> 38:07.118
That's true.

38:07.702 --> 38:08.995
You're so funny.

38:09.662 --> 38:11.247
That's embarrassing.

38:12.248 --> 38:14.625
Yeah, it's embarrassing.

38:17.378 --> 38:18.504
But it made me happy.

38:24.969 --> 38:26.262
How embarrassing.

38:29.098 --> 38:30.725
Are you embarrassed?

38:30.808 --> 38:31.851
So cute.

38:33.019 --> 38:34.186
Whatever.

38:34.770 --> 38:36.439
Communication issues, huh?

38:36.522 --> 38:37.898
PREVIEW

38:37.982 --> 38:39.942
Maybe it is difficult for two people

38:40.026 --> 38:42.028
from different backgrounds to be together?

38:42.111 --> 38:42.945
‪THIS DRAMA IS FICTION AND ALL CHARACTERS
‪AND ORGANIZATIONS ARE FICTIONAL

38:43.029 --> 38:43.904
Subtitle translation by: Kiko Morita
